  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「モモタマナ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%A2%E3%83%A2%E3%82%BF%E3%83%9E%E3%83%8A",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 110111181,
      "text": "モモタマナ Terminalia catappa L. は、シクンシ科に属する樹木。太平洋諸島などに広く分布する。葉が大きく、枝振りが美しいので植栽されることが多い。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Terminalia catappa」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terminalia_catappa",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1370163033,
      "text": "Terminalia catappa is a large tropical tree in the leadwood tree family, Combretaceae, native to Asia, Australia, the Pacific, Madagascar and Seychelles. Common names in English include country almond, Indian almond, Malabar almond, sea almond, tropical almond, beach almond and false kamani."
    }
  },
